{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Make for yourself an ark.</b> He had abundant relief and rescue before Him — so why burden him with this construction? So that the men of the generation of the Flood would see him occupied with it for 120 years, and ask him: What is this to you? And he would say to them: The Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to bring a Flood upon the world — perhaps they will repent." "<b>Gopher wood.</b> That is its name. And why this species? On account of the sulfur that was decreed upon them to obliterate them with it." "<b>Rooms.</b> Dwellings, dwellings for every beast and animal." "<b>With pitch.</b> זֶפֶת ('pitch') in Aramaic. And we find in the Talmud: כּוּפְרָא ('pitch') for the ark of Moses — because the waters were placid, pitch sufficed on the inside and tar on the outside; and furthermore, so that that righteous man would not smell the foul odor of the tar. But here, because of the force of the waters, he pitched it both inside and outside."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:47.713902699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}